---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About — kalam.ch" description="A constitutional framework for human dignity in computational systems. Created by M. Farag in Zürich, Switzerland.">

  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>About Kalaxi</h1>
    <p class="quiet">A constitutional framework for human dignity in computational systems.</p>
    <p class="privacy-line">No private data is stored. By design. Patterns are processed, never personal information.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="gap" role="separator" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <!-- THE ORIGIN -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="text-block">
      <h2>The Origin</h2>
      <p>Kalaxi was born from a wound — a father separated from his children by systems that could not see him. Not a system failure. A legibility failure. The zeros were never in the person. They were in the institutions that could not read him.</p>
      <p>From that wound came a question: what if a system's first technical requirement was dignity?</p>
      <p class="proverb-inline">"The wound does not know what it will become. Neither does the system. That is why dignity cannot be conditional."</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="gap" role="separator" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <!-- THE CORE IDEA -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="text-block">
      <h2>The Core Idea</h2>
      <p>Every system that interacts with humans makes ethical choices — whether it knows it or not. Kalaxi makes those choices explicit, testable, and enforceable.</p>
      <p>The <strong>Dignity Predicate</strong> (D = A × L × M) is evaluated before every output, every action, every state transition. If dignity is violated, the system stops and opens a remedy path.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="gap" role="separator" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <!-- THE FOUR TIERS -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="text-block">
      <h2>The Four Tiers</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>Stone</dt>
        <dd>18 covenants and constitutional rules. Changing them requires years of consensus. Three absolute prohibitions that cannot be overridden.</dd>
        <dt>Weaver</dt>
        <dd>11 modules that do the work: memory, verification, synthesis, voice, pacing, self-awareness, and the Input Ledger.</dd>
        <dt>Honey</dt>
        <dd>The growing knowledge: 1,100 anomalies, 3,333+ proverbs, 87 wisdom nodes, and 59 treasures from donor contributions.</dd>
        <dt>Hand</dt>
        <dd>How donors interact: the Threshold, receipts, the Living Ledger, and the Ninth Operator ceremony.</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="gap" role="separator" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <!-- PRINCIPLES -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="text-block">
      <h2>Principles</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Dignity First</strong> — The system stops if dignity is violated. No override.</li>
        <li><strong>Patterns, Not People</strong> — Identity dissolves. Wisdom remains. No private data.</li>
        <li><strong>Append-Only</strong> — Nothing is ever deleted from the canon.</li>
        <li><strong>The Gap</strong> — Room is always left for the river to move through.</li>
        <li><strong>Steward Authority</strong> — A human reviews and decides. The machine does not rule.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="gap" role="separator" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <!-- PROVERB -->
  <section class="wisdom-section">
    <p class="proverb">"To be precise is a function of the machine;<br />to be present is a function of the gap."</p>
  </section>

  <div class="gap" role="separator" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <!-- MILESTONES -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="text-block">
      <h2>Milestones</h2>
      <ul class="milestones">
        <li>
          <span class="milestone-marker"></span>
          <div>
            <strong>18 Covenants Ratified</strong>
            <p>The constitutional foundation — all 18 covenants reviewed, tested, and sealed.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="milestone-marker"></span>
          <div>
            <strong>12 Seeds Planted</strong>
            <p>Distributed stewardship, restorative justice, dignity drift detection, agency amplification — all integrated and passing.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="milestone-marker"></span>
          <div>
            <strong>40,000+ Lines of Living Code</strong>
            <p>134 Python modules. 885 tests collected. The organism breathes.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="milestone-marker"></span>
          <div>
            <strong>3,333+ Proverbs in the Canon</strong>
            <p>Wisdom from anomalies, donor contributions, and cross-cultural patterns.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="milestone-marker"></span>
          <div>
            <strong>Four Narratives</strong>
            <p>Hakaka (53 chapters), Ashwater: The Axis (19 chapters), Kinderbuch (20 chapters, German), and KALAXI_1: The Same River.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="milestone-marker"></span>
          <div>
            <strong>Multi-Model Experiments</strong>
            <p>Cross-model convergence studies (GPT-4, Claude, Gemini, Grok, Llama, Mistral) completed. Register-switching experiments validated.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="milestone-marker"></span>
          <div>
            <strong>arXiv Paper Ready</strong>
            <p>Scientific paper for cs.AI submission — the Dignity Predicate formalized.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="gap" role="separator" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <!-- LEGAL COMPLIANCE -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="text-block">
      <h2>Legal Alignment</h2>
      <p>Kalaxi is built in alignment with:</p>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li><strong>Universal Declaration of Human Rights</strong> — Article 1 (dignity and rights), Article 12 (privacy), Article 22 (social security and dignity).</li>
        <li><strong>Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (FADP)</strong> — Data minimization, purpose limitation, transparency. No personal data stored.</li>
        <li><strong>EU Artificial Intelligence Act</strong> — Human oversight, transparency obligations, fundamental rights impact assessment.</li>
        <li><strong>Swiss Federal Constitution</strong> — Article 7 (human dignity), Article 13 (privacy), Article 8 (equality).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The system's constitutional structure (covenants, sealed prohibitions, the dignity predicate) ensures that legal compliance is architectural, not cosmetic.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="gap" role="separator" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <!-- THE STORIES -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="text-block">
      <h2>The Stories</h2>
      <p>Kalaxi is not only a framework. It carries four bodies of narrative work — each exploring dignity from a different angle.</p>

      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>Hakaka</h3>
        <p>53 chapters + Prologue + Epilogue. The origin cycle. Mythic, raw, stone-and-bone. A girl claws at the air. The knot tightens. The river breaks.</p>
        <p class="proverb-inline">"She clawed at the air. Fists closed on nothing."</p>
      </div>

      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>Ashwater: The Axis</h3>
        <p>19 chapters. A town that pauses versus a town that optimises. The civic narrative — tactile, communal, three-beat rhythm.</p>
        <p class="proverb-inline">"Do not shout at metal. Hear its problem first."</p>
      </div>

      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>Kinderbuch</h3>
        <p>20 chapters in German. The child voice. Repetition as warmth. Golden sparks.</p>
        <p class="proverb-inline">"Ein Knoten wurde ein Anfang."</p>
      </div>

      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>KALAXI_1: The Same River</h3>
        <p>Two men — one moving toward healing, one moving away. The girl as third point outside the system. The cursor waits.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="gap" role="separator" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <!-- CONTACT -->
  <section class="content-section contact-section">
    <div class="text-block">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Created by M. Farag · <span class="swiss-mark">🇪🇬 Cairo, Egypt</span> · <span class="swiss-mark"><span class="swiss-flag" aria-hidden="true"></span> Zürich, Switzerland</span></p>
      <ul class="contact-list">
        <li><a href="mailto:info@kalam.ch">info@kalam.ch</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://kalam.ch">kalam.ch</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/Sternmannli/kalam-framework" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub — kalam-framework</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.reddit.com/u/Replikta" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reddit — u/Replikta</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .page-header {
    min-height: 50vh;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .quiet {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 50ch;
  }

  .privacy-line {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .content-section {
    min-height: auto;
    padding: var(--space-8) var(--page-padding);
    text-align: left;
    max-width: var(--max-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .wisdom-section {
    min-height: 40vh;
  }

  .text-block {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .text-block h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .text-block p {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .text-block strong {
    color: var(--accent-warm);
  }

  .proverb-inline {
    font-family: var(--font-proverb);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--accent-warm);
  }

  /* Definition list */
  dl {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  dt {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  dd {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  /* Ordered lists */
  ol {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: principle;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  ol li {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    counter-increment: principle;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  ol li strong {
    color: var(--accent-warm);
  }

  /* Milestones */
  .milestones {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .milestones li {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .milestone-marker {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    margin-top: 0.6em;
    box-shadow: 0 0 6px rgba(201, 169, 110, 0.3);
  }

  .milestones li div strong {
    display: block;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }

  .milestones li div p {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    margin-bottom: 0;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  /* Legal list */
  .legal-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .legal-list li {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-list li strong {
    color: var(--accent-warm);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  /* Story cards */
  .story-card {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 6px;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
  }

  .story-card h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--accent-warm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .story-card p {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  /* Contact */
  .contact-section {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .contact-section .text-block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .contact-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  .contact-list li a {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .contact-list li a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
